{:edb/db-before-t 2323 :edb/db-after-t 2324 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535636 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:11:33.439Z" 13194139535636 true] [17592186064164 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358667 13194139535636 true] [17592186064165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358653 13194139535636 true] [17592186064165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358670 13194139535636 true] [17592186064166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358660 13194139535636 true] [17592186064864 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535636 true] [17592186064864 1100 "Consider the function $f(x) = x\\ln (x - 4)$. Given that $y = f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $(f^{-1})^{′}(0)$." 13194139535636 false] [17592186064864 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4).$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186064864 1145 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(0).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(0)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(0) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =0 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard $x=0$ since the logarithm is not defined here. Therefore, ${f}^{-1}(0)=5.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(5),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4)+\\frac{x}{x-4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5-4)+\\frac{5}{5-4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358654 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1089 "q-110284" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1100 "The following table gives the values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3)$ of the product of functions.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $-3$ |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $2$ |" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1113 #uuid "b4e4e308-8907-50e5-ac2c-e0df07b3b6b7" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358653 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nUsing this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function ${f}^{-1}(x)g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(x)=\\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}+{g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3)=\\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3).\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=-2,$ $g(3)=-1,$ ${g}^{′}(3)=-3,$ and ${f}^{′}(-2)=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3) & =\\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{{f}^{′}(-2)}+(-3)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-5}+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358655 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358656 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358657 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358658 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358659 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1041 "selection" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358656 13194139535636 true] [17592186358654 1110 #uuid "0307a327-bfa9-5d9e-af9a-20a228fb4cd0" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358655 1034 "-5" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358655 1111 #uuid "00fd7ea9-c5cf-5491-8b4d-07208bb52a63" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358656 1034 "\\frac{31}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358656 1111 #uuid "1c5b4e62-b0ab-5606-a50e-773260737de5" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358657 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358657 1111 #uuid "a576bfeb-f50e-5d34-b75d-b4f735112802" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358658 1034 "6" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358658 1111 #uuid "00f0cf9c-938f-5535-8a8f-976a1870e794" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358659 1034 "-\\frac{44}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358659 1111 #uuid "18e14d21-b6c3-5982-a761-c3ddc12633b5" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358661 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1089 "q-110347" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=-3+5{e}^{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2).$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1113 #uuid "db615c68-58b9-59cf-a49b-080adcb0dc8f" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358660 1145 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =2 \\\\ -3+5{e}^{x+1} & =2 \\\\ 5{e}^{x+1} & =5 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =1 \\\\ x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(2)=-1.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(-1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-3+5{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =5{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =5{e}^{0} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358662 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358663 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358664 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358665 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358666 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1041 "selection" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358664 13194139535636 true] [17592186358661 1110 #uuid "5861a3c0-d5a2-5dcc-b42d-0b4f16c4e9c4" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358662 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358662 1111 #uuid "9cc808bf-2179-5e7b-a79d-c5ea3ac5270d" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358663 1034 "-\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358663 1111 #uuid "1aba46c3-a1db-57c3-a68f-5042be559f03" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358664 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358664 1111 #uuid "af31f27e-8dd0-5ad0-b54b-9190421b3bb2" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358665 1034 "5" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358665 1111 #uuid "37445c44-a558-548e-b880-ae365bd0f358" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358666 1034 "-2" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358666 1111 #uuid "d7efbf48-9657-5d03-90a0-8c5167d4dfc3" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358668 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1089 "q-312581" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{3x-2}{x+2}$ and the point $P(-1,-5)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ the slope of $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ at the point $(-5,-1)$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1113 #uuid "cebaf180-0ec8-5580-ae72-a70d7fc75656" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358667 1145 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(-1,-5).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3x-2}{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{8}{(x+2)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =8\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(-1,-5)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(-5,-1)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(-5) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-5))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358669 13194139535636 true] [17592186358668 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535636 true] [17592186358668 1041 "field-1" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358668 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358669 13194139535636 true] [17592186358668 1110 #uuid "62d7696f-552c-513c-98d7-7ef24cade1db" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358669 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358669 1111 #uuid "6c5b27cc-72ce-5757-983e-126e34951310" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358671 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1089 "q-75832" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1100 "The following table gives the values of functions $g(x)$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({g}^{-1})^{′}(7).$\n\n| **$x$** | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $9$ | $-1$ |\n| $4$ | $7$ | $-4$ |" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1113 #uuid "33a013a9-ba3a-57f2-9361-b990abac67ee" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358670 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=7,$ we have\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{′}(7)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(7))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${g}^{-1}(7)=4$ and ${g}^{′}(4)=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({g}^{-1})^{′}(7) & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(7))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358672 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358673 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358674 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358675 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358676 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1041 "selection" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358675 13194139535636 true] [17592186358671 1110 #uuid "ebf66df6-87fa-53e7-8d28-476241693f2b" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358672 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358672 1111 #uuid "f7b4f9f9-3f99-563e-bee5-09b39040d4f9" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358673 1034 "\\frac{1}{7}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358673 1111 #uuid "294dfcb7-bdaf-5a95-8a74-13259c3185f2" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358674 1034 "\\frac{1}{9}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358674 1111 #uuid "a4cc340a-eb97-5670-bf4e-8eabcde19bbd" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358675 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535636 true] [17592186358675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535636 true] [17592186358675 1111 #uuid "7f8f096d-c958-504d-89c3-b044a8399e1c" 13194139535636 true] [1